<speak>
<s>This is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">29042026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Abu Dhabi is leaving <sub alias="oh-peck">OPEC</sub> after fifty-seven years, effective May first, shattering Gulf oil unity at the worst possible moment.</s> <s>Iran's blockade of the Strait of Hormuz has erased thirteen point seven million barrels a day from global supply, Goldman Sachs says, dissolving the logic of cartel production caps for the Emirates.</s> <s>Freed from quota constraints, Abu Dhabi can now pump at will into a market the cartel was built to discipline.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Papua New Guinea's national court has cleared Starlink to operate, ending a two-year licensing block by the country's anti-corruption Ombudsman.</s> <s>The judges ruled the watchdog exceeded its constitutional authority when it vetoed telecom permits.</s> <s>China's Huawei dominates terrestrial connectivity across the South Pacific — now SpaceX has the spectrum, and who controls Pacific connectivity is a great-power question a Port Moresby courtroom has just begun to answer.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>India's Election Commission has struck nine point one million voters from West Bengal's rolls — twelve percent of the state's electorate, with Muslims removed disproportionately, the Sabar Institute found.</s> <s>Bengal is the longest-eluded prize in Modi's electoral map, and Mamata Banerjee's Trinamool Congress is the last regional firewall against Hindutva politics.</s> <s>Results land May fourth; if Trinamool holds, India's federal opposition still has a state-level breakwater. If it falls, the wall is gone.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Two months after a US missile struck a school next to a Revolutionary Guard base in Iran, the Pentagon still won't say whether the school was on the pre-planned target list.</s> <s>Former defence officials tell the BBC that length of silence is anomalous — Washington normally claims a clean strike within hours, even on contested ones.</s> <s>No inquiry has opened, and the children killed remain unnamed in any official American accounting.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Pakistan deployed fighter jets to Saudi Arabia on April eleventh while US-Iran talks ran quietly in Islamabad.</s> <s>Its nuclear deterrent and six-hundred-thousand-strong army give Islamabad leverage no Gulf state can match — positioning Pakistan as a third security pillar alongside Riyadh and Ankara.</s> <s>The Gulf order that for fifty years rested on American guarantees is being rewritten in sha'Allah by its junior partners.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Syrian forces have arrested Amjad Youssef, the man filmed in twenty-thirteen executing forty-one civilians into a pit in the Tadamon district of Damascus.</s> <s>Internal Security tracked him for thirty days before seizing him at his family home in Hama.</s> <s>It's the first domestic prosecution of a regime-era mass killer since Assad's fall — a test of whether transitional justice in Damascus is procedural or political.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Indonesia has ordered one hundred fifty million barrels of Russian crude as the Iran war collapses Gulf throughput.</s> <s>Moscow has signed crude and fertiliser deals across four Southeast Asian states this month, despite explicit European sanctions warnings.</s> <s>Brussels says <sub alias="ah-see-an">ASEAN</sub> is funding Moscow's war chest; Jakarta replies that a rice paddy can't run on a Western foreign policy preference.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Russian fuel entered Bangladesh's first nuclear reactor on Tuesday at the Rooppur plant, which Rosatom built on eleven point nine billion dollars of Moscow's sovereign debt.</s> <s>Russia will supply the uranium and manage the spent waste for the next sixty years, and Dhaka projects a billion dollars in annual fuel-import savings.</s> <s>A hundred and seventy million Muslims have just chosen a Russian reactor at the height of Western sanctions on Rosatom — and locked their grid into Moscow's orbit for two generations.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Russia is halting Kazakh crude through the Druzhba pipeline to Germany from May first.</s> <s>The PCK Schwedt refinery near Berlin — already running on Kazakh transit after sanctions cut Russian crude in twenty-twenty-three — faces a forty-three-thousand-barrel-a-day supply gap.</s> <s>Berlin is in talks for emergency tanker imports through Rostock... an expensive substitute for a pipeline that ran for sixty years.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Canada has become the first Group of Seven country to approve a generic version of semaglutide, the diabetes and weight-loss drug sold as Ozempic.</s> <s>Health Canada cleared an Indian manufacturer's version at forty-five to ninety percent below the brand price.</s> <s>Indian generics have broken Western monopolies on HIV and hepatitis drugs before; semaglutide is the first metabolic blockbuster to face the same pressure, and the price collapse will spread.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Europe warmed at twice the global average through twenty-twenty-five, the World Meteorological Organization reported, with record wildfires, glacial melt, and marine heatwaves stretching into northern seas.</s> <s>Renewables reached forty-six percent of the continent's electricity, but emissions still didn't fall fast enough to bend the trajectory.</s> <s>Europe is no longer near the global climate mean — it's a faster-warming continent, breaking the planning baselines its agriculture, infrastructure, and energy systems were all built on.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Pacific island states that import nearly all their liquid fuel are buckling under Iran-war oil prices.</s> <s>Clinics are running on stand-by power, school days are being cut, and several governments have ordered emergency rationing of diesel for grid generation.</s> <s>The fastest shift to solar microgrids in Pacific history is now under way — driven not by climate negotiation, but by a price shock no climate summit ever delivered.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Microsoft and OpenAI have unwound the exclusive revenue-share contract that defined the generative AI era.</s> <s>Microsoft no longer takes a cut of OpenAI's revenue, and OpenAI is no longer required to host exclusively on Azure.</s> <s>The keystone deal of the twenty-twenty-three to twenty-twenty-five capital cycle is gone, and who pays for the next compute build-out — and who controls model distribution — is suddenly an open question.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Six hundred million Africans cannot use artificial intelligence tools, the International Energy Agency reports.</s> <s>Internet access alone costs more than a quarter of monthly wages across Sub-Saharan Africa, and daily power cuts sever the connections the technology requires.</s> <s>Electrification is trailing population growth, locking the region out of the productivity gains the rest of the world is capturing — a digital divide widening into a continental fault line.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The International Rescue Committee is deploying purpose-built AI agents to triage information requests from refugees in Sudan, eastern Congo, and the Rohingya camps, where caseworker capacity has collapsed under demand.</s> <s>The trade-off the sector has accepted is stark — an imperfect answer about asylum or shelter, the committee concluded, beats no answer at all.</s> <s>What 'good enough' means when the alternative is silence is now a humanitarian design question with no precedent.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>